<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phyllis</span></b> , ĭdis and
		ĭdos, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φυλλίς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Daughter of King Sithon of Thrace; she was changed
				into an almond-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 2,
			98</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 59, 243</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				26, 45, § 108</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Serv.
				Verg. E. 5, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 1,
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>an
			almond-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall. Insit. 149</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A female proper name</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 3,
				78</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4, 11, 3</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Dom. 17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
